WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.060
The dragon capsule on crew 13 docked at the International Space Station seven hours and 55 minutes after liftoff. This is SpaceX Daily, episode 118, a new core stage flew for the first time on falcon heavy during the NRL 97 mission. The vehicle lifted off from LC39A at 11.54pm Eastern daylight time on October 1st on a northeasterly trajectory.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:35.180
side-booster B-1104 flew its second mission and landed at LZ-1 while B-1072

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:42.160
flew its fourth mission and landed at LZ-2. Core stage B-1106 flew once and was

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:47.160
expended. The flight marked the 14th Falcon Heavy launch and the first National

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:54.240
Reconnaissance Office mission under the 2025 NSSL Phase 3 Lane 2 contract. Crew

00:00:54.240 --> 00:01:00.060
13 set the new US record for the fastest trip to the station. Commander Jessica Watkins

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:05.440
became the first black woman to command a spacecraft during orbital insertion. Pilot

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:11.600
Luke Delaney joined Canadian astronaut Joshua Kutrick and Ross Cosmos Cosmonaut Sergei

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:19.000
Teter-Yatnikov on the four-person crew. Booster B1101 flew its third mission and landed at

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:25.740
LZ40. A joint Ryan Metal and Argo Tech satellite reached orbit on a Falcon 9 from Vandenberg

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:31.280
on October 1st. The spacecraft will detect ground indicators of airborne threats and

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:37.560
route AI-process data straight into national air defense command systems. The launch begins Ryan

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:44.070
Metal's satellite-based situational awareness capability. Four Google Trillium chips flew aboard a

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:50.190
at labs satellite on Transporter 18. Engineers shook the satellite on all axes and exposed

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:55.230
the chips to proton beams before flight to qualify them for launch loads and radiation.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:02:00.090
Contact was confirmed shortly after launch and commissioning is now underway.

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:05.930
University of Memphis Professor Chun-Rung Jiya started measuring air quality and noise

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:12.450
around the XAI Colossus site. The study responds to rapid growth of multiple data center projects

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:17.310
in the region. Dredging has begun on the Canal Network at Starbase, Louisiana.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:22.750
Workers are widening small canals originally dug by humble oil that connect to the larger

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:28.990
Bayou Freshwater Canal to improve construction access. A golden dragon plush served as the

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:35.650
0G indicator on Crew 13. Observers watch the toy float during the live NASA docking broadcast.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:42.130
Kyrgyz Republic President Sadir Joparov viewed the transporter-18 lift-off from Vandenberg

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:42.830
in person.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:46.930
The visit coincided with the launch of Kyrgyzstan's first satellite.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:52.650
Reddit users posted multiple images of the Falcon Heavy Night launch shortly after midnight.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:57.490
Footage of side-booster separation and landing burns drew particular attention.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:04.330
One thing worth watching is the $830 million sequestration cut now facing unspent defense

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:09.830
reconciliation funds. Space and missile defense lines funded through the bill could see reduced

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:15.830
buying power, though the Pentagon has not identified which accounts are short. The outcome depends

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:21.430
on whether Congress restores the funds or accepts the automatic reduction. On the AI front,

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:27.590
the Orbital TPU test continues to run through initial commissioning. The Google TPU test satellite

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:32.750
illustrates the core thermal and radiation constraints of orbital compute. In vacuum,

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:38.870
heat can only leave through radiation or conduction along heat pipes, so the team's sized radiators

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:42.330
to keep junction temperatures inside the trillium operating window.

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:48.810
Each chip must survive 50-100G launch loads and cumulative proton fluids that can flip

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:49.650
bits in memory.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:55.310
Pre-flight proton beam tests quantify the error rate and the mitigation code that will run

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:55.850
on orbit.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:04:01.610
If the four chip stack stays within power and thermal limits, the next design step becomes

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:07.410
a larger array linked by optical inter-satellite links that could move raw training data at tens

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:13.030
of terabits per second without ground stations. That architecture trades the high cost of lifting

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:17.730
mass for the eight-fold increase in solar energy available in sun-synchronous orbit.

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:22.750
Exactly the trade's SpaceX's starship mass to orbit numbers are meant to improve.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:29.630
The idiot index here is the ratio of finished satellite cost to the raw silicon solar cells and

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:30.750
aluminum radiator mass.

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:33.510
Every gram of radiation shielding

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:36.450
or extra radiator area multiplies that index

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:39.530
until reuse or higher launch cadence brings it down.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:43.710
A quick look at the tape shows S and PCX closing lower.

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:46.990
Before we go, the next Falcon 9 ride share

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:49.550
from Vandenberg is already in final countdown.

